sanctioned: this program exercises the Ipe.Db.Dsn parse-don't-validate surface, an Ipê-only addition with no counterpart in the reference backend, so a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both; Ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. It is PURE — it parses/builds descriptors and prints, performing no database connection or I/O beyond stdout. The five output lines assert, in order: (1) a valid Postgres DSN carrying a password parses, and its Driver, host, and default TLS mode plus its REDACTED render are printed — the password NEVER appears (it is a Secret; the render substitutes "[redacted]"); (2) an explicit "sslmode=disable" is a hard typed Err (fail-closed TLS — a Dsn is never a proof of a cleartext transport); (3) an explicit "sslmode=require", which does not verify the server certificate, is a hard typed Err; (4) a DSN that omits sslmode defaults to "verify-full" (the secure default); (5) Dsn.build from typed parts runs the same validators and yields a descriptor. The password sentinel "hunter2SENTINEL" is deliberately absent from every line, proving the Secret non-leak invariant end-to-end through the emitted crate.
